{"id":55564,"ord":16,"n_segments":90,"prev":55563,"next":55565,"doc":{"id":"68090","title":"68090_Ed Garland oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Ed Garland","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68090/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68090"},"chapter":"From New Orleans to Chicago","title":"Chicago jobs: the luncheonette and Manuel Perez's band","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"After the show closed he played for Isadora Shaw, then with Perez at Paulina and Madison where two bands shared a gangster-run house.","period":"1910s","year_from":1910,"year_to":1919,"words":217,"start":[27,15],"end":[29,16],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68090#s55564","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Chicago","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"Paulina Street","focus":1,"type":"street","in":"Chicago"},{"name":"Madison Street","focus":1,"type":"street","in":"Chicago"}],"venues":[{"name":"Luncheonette","focus":1,"city":"Chicago"},{"name":"Dreamland","focus":0,"city":"Chicago"}],"bands":[{"name":"Manuel Perez's band","focus":1,"leader":"Manuel Perez"},{"name":"Red Nichols's band","focus":1,"leader":"Red Nichols"}]},"people":[{"name":"Manuel Perez","qid":"Q1701748","n":6},{"name":"Louis Cottrell","qid":"Q6686935","n":2},{"name":"Red Nichols","qid":"Q495464","n":2},{"name":"Ed Garland","qid":"Q1282347","n":1},{"name":"Eddie Atkins","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Isadora Shaw","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"PAULINA","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Madison","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Lorenzo Tio","qid":"Q1262225","n":1},{"name":"Frankie Enger","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":33,"theme_name":"Chicago: the jazz migration and its clubs","community":59,"community_name":"Going north: working the Chicago jazz scene","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":27,"b":15,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Well, that closed and Isadora Shaw got me to play for her at Dreamland. Not Dreamland. It's the Dreamland later on."},{"p":28,"b":0,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":28,"b":1,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"At the Luncheonette."},{"p":28,"b":2,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"I see. And then did you get together with Manuel Perez in a band?"},{"p":28,"b":3,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Well --"},{"p":28,"b":4,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"At this time."},{"p":28,"b":5,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"-- Manuel was playing out on PAULINA, and -- with Red Nichols."},{"p":28,"b":6,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":28,"b":7,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"They was playing in one corner and Manuel and them was playing in the other corner. Two bands in the house, you know?"},{"p":28,"b":8,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":28,"b":9,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Out on PAULINA. And Madison."},{"p":28,"b":10,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":28,"b":11,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And I played out there with Manuel. He had an awful band out there. Manuel got me to play with him."},{"p":28,"b":12,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":28,"b":13,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Manuel was in Chicago. Manuel was rolling -- making cigars."},{"p":28,"b":14,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"That's right."},{"p":28,"b":15,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"During the day, you know."},{"p":28,"b":16,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yes."},{"p":28,"b":17,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Played at PAULINA and Madison."},{"p":29,"b":0,"s":"","x":"HEMLOCK ERASABLE COTTON CONTENT"},{"p":29,"b":1,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh. At night."},{"p":29,"b":2,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And I played out there with him. And he had Manuel Perez played trumpet. Eddie Atkins playing trombone. Lorenzo To playing clarinet."},{"p":29,"b":3,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":29,"b":4,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Frankie [Enger] playing piano. Cantrell playing drums."},{"p":29,"b":5,"s":"","x":"[Cottrell]"},{"p":29,"b":6,"s":"","x":"[Ahayau] [Gushee Horns]"},{"p":29,"b":7,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":29,"b":8,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And I was playing the bass."},{"p":29,"b":9,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"The bass."},{"p":29,"b":10,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Ed Garland played bass."},{"p":29,"b":11,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Right."},{"p":29,"b":12,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"That was some band, too."},{"p":29,"b":13,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Yeah."},{"p":29,"b":14,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"Red Nichols band was playing."},{"p":29,"b":15,"s":"MR. TURETSKY","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":29,"b":16,"s":"MR. GARLAND","x":"And that was a bad place. That was out there among some gangsters, where we was playing there."}]}